<DocsLayout
  title="ACP compatibility"
  eyebrow="Protocols"
  description="Run Roder as an Agent Client Protocol agent over stdio."
  prev={{ href: "/docs/app-server/", title: "App server" }}
>
  <p>
    <code>roder acp</code> starts a native Rust
    <a href="https://agentclientprotocol.com/">Agent Client Protocol</a> endpoint over
    stdio JSON-RPC. It uses the same app-server runtime, tools, and policy decisions as
    other Roder clients and implements the stable ACP v1 wire protocol.
  </p>

  <h2>Start the agent</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/docs/install/">Install Roder</a> and configure your
    <a href="/docs/providers/">inference provider</a> before starting the agent.
    Configure your ACP client to launch the <code>roder</code> executable with
    <code>acp</code> as its argument. The executable must be available on the client's
    <code>PATH</code>; otherwise, use its absolute path.
  </p>

  <pre><code>roder acp</code></pre>

  <p>To run from a source checkout:</p>
  <pre><code>cargo run -p roder -- acp</code></pre>

  <h2>Sessions and prompt turns</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>initialize</code> negotiates ACP v1 and reports baseline session support.</li>
    <li><code>session/new</code> creates a Roder thread for an absolute <code>cwd</code>.</li>
    <li><code>session/prompt</code> accepts text and resource links and starts a turn.</li>
    <li><code>session/cancel</code> interrupts the active turn.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    During a prompt turn, <code>session/update</code> notifications stream assistant
    text, reasoning text, and tool-call progress. Protected tool calls send
    <code>session/request_permission</code> requests to the client with
    <code>allow_once</code> and <code>reject_once</code> options.
  </p>

  <p>
    Send <code>session/cancel</code> as a notification. The outstanding
    <code>session/prompt</code> request returns <code>stopReason: "cancelled"</code>
    after the turn ends.
  </p>

  <h2>Current limits</h2>
  <p>
    Roder does not advertise session loading, listing, deletion, resumption, or closing
    through ACP. Unsupported optional methods return JSON-RPC method-not-found.
    <code>session/new</code> rejects nonempty <code>additionalDirectories</code> and
    <code>mcpServers</code> lists. MCP servers cannot be attached through ACP.
  </p>

  <p>
    Image, audio, and embedded-resource prompt blocks are unsupported. Tool updates can
    include screenshots when computer-use tools are enabled; this does not enable image
    prompts.
  </p>

  <p>
    Use <a href="/docs/app-server/">the native app-server JSON-RPC API</a> for Roder's
    lifecycle, recovery, drain, and ownership diagnostics. Those details are not exposed
    as ACP capabilities.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
